# Everything has a default that fits a stock demonstrator started with `docker compose up` in the folder above:
# the Keycloak address, realm, client secrets and admin account are read from ../.env (the file docker compose reads).
# Copy this file to .env only to change something.

# --- Target ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API as the browser sees it: the web server of the demonstrator proxies /api to the API container.
# E2E_API_URL=http://localhost:5173/api
# Keycloak (the demonstrator serves a self-signed certificate on 8443: accept it for the test)
# E2E_KEYCLOAK_URL=https://0.0.0.0:8443
E2E_INSECURE_TLS=1

# --- Accounts -------------------------------------------------------------------
# By default the test creates two accounts in the realm (the realm ships with no human user), with the roles
# submitter and admin-fega, and sets a fresh random password on every run (kept in memory only).
# It needs the admin account of Keycloak: KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME / _PASSWORD of ../.env.
# E2E_MANAGE_ACCOUNTS=1
# E2E_SUBMITTER_USERNAME=e2e-submitter
# E2E_SUBMITTER_EMAIL=e2e-submitter@example.org
# E2E_HELPDESK_USERNAME=e2e-helpdesk
# E2E_HELPDESK_EMAIL=e2e-helpdesk@example.org
# With E2E_MANAGE_ACCOUNTS=0 use existing accounts: E2E_<SUBMITTER|HELPDESK>_USERNAME + E2E_<...>_PASSWORD (or a ready E2E_<...>_TOKEN)
# The client of the user logins (needs Direct access grants) and of the DAC decisions
# E2E_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=fhdportal-cli
# E2E_DAC_CLIENT_ID=dac-cli

# --- Test data and the fake SDA -------------------------------------------------------
# E2E_GENERATOR=./create_test_bundle.php
# fega-cli, or "php /path/to/fhdportal-api/bin/fega.phar"
# E2E_FEGA_CLI=fega-cli
# E2E_PATIENTS=2
# The inbox folder that the API container mounts (the files go to <folder>/<e-mail of the submitter>/)
# E2E_SDA_INBOX=../sda-inbox
# Run the cron jobs of the API container at once (docker compose exec) instead of waiting for the next minute
# E2E_TRIGGER_CRON=1

# --- Scenario -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The policy of the mock DAC portal
# E2E_POLICY_TITLE="Standard Data Access Policy"
# Statuses of an access request that mean "approved"
# E2E_REQUEST_ACCEPTED=APR,approved
# Force values of the access request form, as JSON
# E2E_REQUEST_FORM_JSON='{"title":"..."}'
# Minutes to wait for the uploaded files, the approval of the submission (cron job) and the catalogue
# E2E_FILES_TIMEOUT_MIN=4
# E2E_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_MIN=4
# E2E_CATALOGUE_TIMEOUT_MIN=2
# Minutes to wait for the dataset in the Beacon (its model is cached for 5 minutes; the test drops it when docker compose works)
# E2E_BEACON_TIMEOUT_MIN=6
